      "message": "One subtle issue with this approach is that it doing things in a wrong place i.e. it tailors view holder for the data set at view holder\u0027s creation vs at view binding. Logically, a view holder can be created once and bound multiple times - I can only imagine a hypothetical scenario when package installation triggers data update and instead of one direct share target we\u0027re now getting two and binding it to a view holder that was created to handle only one.\nIn practice, though, there\u0027s have only one view of each affected type and empirically package installation (or pinned status change) triggers a new view holder creation. Even more, forcing view holder recycling (through a custom view pool) breaks the UI!\nRegardless, I think it would be better to adjust the UI at binding somehow; I\u0027ll look into it a bit more.",
